ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412185 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "77f278fd-49bc-544f-84b1-fa3bfe926285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412186 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7f638fd3-87cf-5489-b15f-bb90365aa5c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412189 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca8f622f-5689-5e59-b05c-8fbe8f53d165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412190 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e818f6e1-d129-5503-b9af-07473e5656ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412192 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f31a7306-1b8a-5b78-bf95-372025264fa5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surfaces $x=-{z}^{2}$ and $x=\\sqrt{y},$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=1,$ $z=-1,$ $z=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "248b6467-c247-56b8-869d-ac65691d4383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412193 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,-{z}^{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-{z}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[x]_{x=-{z}^{2}}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-(-{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[z\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-1}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-(-1))\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\sqrt{y}+3\\,dy \\\\  & ={[2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}+3y]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}+3(1)-0 \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/da/daedf62c68ba62dee844cf17efc2d767da47a06ceccaedde854779f542b90114.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front and right ones, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c5e175a-7b49-566c-a1ad-cebab486783a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412194 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/7c/7c1738e97bc16a32f86d6901136afc4d9e288035d170fcd640db340ad36d19c5.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $z=z(y),$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation $x=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z:$\n\n$$\n1=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\,⟹\\,z=2-\\frac{2}{3}y\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea8b8397163309a11aa478fcc21ab53ee293c19f0d77a93b5c3d3472bb0eba70.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3-z/2}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}(2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2})-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2-\\frac{y}{3})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-2y/3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2-\\frac{y}{3})(2-\\frac{2y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}{(2-\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})((2-\\frac{y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(2-\\frac{2y}{3}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})(\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{6})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3-\\frac{4y}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[3y-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{27}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(3(3)-\\frac{2(3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{27})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3fb0f5ed-20e1-5a6f-bec1-d9ddd1ad73da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412196 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le x\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane and the plane $z=x+y+2,$ and the planes $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ddd03f9-52bb-5aac-ab6f-e8e23245dd8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412199 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le x+y+2\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x+y+2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x+y+2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x+y+2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[(x+2)y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+2+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}x]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =0-(\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le 1+x,\\,0\\le z\\le xy\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89162549-49ec-507f-b56c-dea9e66a6c30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412201 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}[z]_{z=0}^{z=xy}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1-x}^{y=1+x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+x)^{2}-(1-x)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+2x+{x}^{2})-(1-2x+{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}(4x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161661" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,4\\le z\\le 8-x,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-\\frac{x}{2}\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b5b7d1e-4726-5549-b494-2d265b26d8f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412202 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}2-\\frac{x}{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2}){[z]}_{z=4}^{z=8-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(8-x-4)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(4-x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}8-4x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[8x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=4} \\\\  & =(8(4)-2(4)^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}(4)^{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $x=5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=9-4{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5335202-1eb7-59f8-9c44-3e9c073e7a32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412206 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 9-4{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{9-4{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-4{y}^{2})-(5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}\\,9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161698" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc1d5c0b-7b74-5ad3-bb28-1b0236b6db17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412207 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/9e/9e7c6fad45d9d85bad5ca16a2000e4d44a1739ab70797e41ae94945a4ffb02ef.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/2-z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x/2-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{x}{2}-z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3-\\frac{x}{2})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3-\\frac{x}{2})(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8-2)-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161691" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b0/b0645201b3726750226811e0c714dc09d3075021fcbb6ddd1525748e9539c02d.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d44ebfc0-d493-5ede-9c33-adfa1ab81dd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412209 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/c4/c4cf12ec9b53282620c1730f824c96d98e0b9dbabee0478bf258cf6c2741da81.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b497e6ef73b5b16e11baa08819e9628d3b5e1f2ee4d05fbafec48f73e087cbf1.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=1+y+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+y+z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(1+y)z+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}+y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428559 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428559 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band cros